  "authoringNote": "The final encounter and final order state the same date. Only the order states an explicit time; the encounter is date-only. SPEC Data contracts forbid inventing an encounter completion time from a date-only record, and C02 requires both sources to state explicit times, so the late-afternoon order time does not establish the sequence: the pair holds R04.same_day_unsequenced, manual_review for the administrative reviewer. R04 cites the encounter status, date and practitioner identifier and the order status, date, timestamp and practitioner identifier (seven) and names no parent (C07). R05 compares the receipt with the stated order timestamp (2026-09-02T23:00:00Z in UTC): 2026-09-03T17:05:00Z is after it, so the receipt follows (C06) and R05 passes, citing the receipt reference and time, the order date and the order timestamp (five). R01, R02, R03, R07, R08 and R09 pass, R06 is qualified clinical review with five clinical citations and no administrative effect, and R10 is not applicable. The state is needs_human_review.",
